      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture. The original test has several understandability issues: many unused imports, and all assertions are packed into one method with no explanatory structure. I'll produce a cleaner version with only the needed imports, inline comments grouping assertions by behavior, and a clearer expression of the platform-dependent `SYSTEM` assertions.Now I'll compile-check the generated file.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored file removes all unused imports (leaving only `assertEquals`, `assertTrue`, `File`, and `@Test`), and adds concise inline comments that group the nine assertions by the three `IOCase` variants (`SENSITIVE`, `INSENSITIVE`, `SYSTEM`), making the intent of each block immediately clear to a reader."
